  "query_preview": "/Thursday through Monday/...\nIssued 314 AM MDT MON JUL 20 2026\nThe pattern will shift once again during the extended. On \nThursday, an upper level trough off the Pacific Northwest coast \nwill begin to deepen, turning the flow aloft southwesterly. This\nwill push monsoonal moisture to the east and usher in a much \ndrier airmass. Shower/storm chances will decrease through the \nend of the week, and by Sunday will be less than 20% in all \nareas. Southwest flow will keep temperatures hot, with lower \nvalley highs in the upper 90s to around 100 degrees. The trough \nwill bring breezy conditions each day with gusts 15-30 mph. \nSmoke may impact the area through the period, especially across\nsoutheast Oregon.",
